<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Comontorius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 277 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Comontorius was the leader of a band of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/celts">Celts</a> who took part in the invasion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a> in 279 BCE and then settled in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polybius">Polybius</a>, they founded a kingdom with its capital at Tylis around 277 BCE. His kingdom forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> to pay heavy tribute.</p></div>
